{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews","id":1279952,"title":"[2E] New Purviews","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-10T13:07:02-08:00","id":1279952,"title":"[2E] New Purviews","content":"So after reading the <b>Scion 2E Hero</b>, I found I miss some parts of Gods in Pantheons shown. And as we are A LOT of time till <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279418-scion-2e-demigod-official\"><b>2E Demigod</b></a>, I think some fan made Purviews are in order. I dearly miss those\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Knowledge</b></span><br /> <br /> Gods of Knowledge are popular in all major Pantheons and it\u2019s weird there isn\u2019t Purview of it. It would probably have Boons based on automatic Success on Mental rolls? ( In <b>CoD</b> it would be simply Mental Skills, but in <b>Storypath</b> system Skills are not tied to any particular Arena, so connecting to Mental Attributes. )<br /> <br /> <b>Example Gods: </b>Odin ( Aesir ), Thoth ( Djehuty - Netjar ), Ogma ( Tuatha De Danann )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve missed the Purview of Magic, as for some deities it\u2019s very important title for each of them. Thing is, as general Marvels mechanics just leaves this Purview useless, as ANY God can make ANY Marvel from their Purview. :/ I was hoping for making Boon like emulating other Purviews Boons by extensive rituals or to counter other Boons \u2013 but with Marvels mechanics it\u2019s just loose sense, in my POV. Maybe you have some way to put Magic as special Purview?<br /> <br /> <b>Example Gods: </b>Odin ( Aesir ), Thoth ( Djehuty - Netjar ), Veles ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">Bogi</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-10-2019, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T13:25:38-08:00","id":1279958,"title":"","content":"1E tried a magic purview. It didn\u2019t work because there\u2019s no definition to designate \u201cmagic\u201d from other miracles one can evoke at will.<br /> <br /> As it stands most PSPs are their corresponding culture\u2019s view of \u201cmagic\u201d. Odin has more in the way of Wyrd Boons than other members of his Pantheon, Aset has more in the way of Heku Boons, etc.<br /> <br /> That and combining any given flashy Marvel with their Pantheon Motif.<br /> <br /> Most of the gods of magic you are talking about have their mental effects supported by the Sage Calling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T13:53:28-08:00","id":1279963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews#post1279952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magic</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve missed the Purview of Magic, as for some deities it\u2019s very important title for each of them. Thing is, as general Marvels mechanics just leaves this Purview useless, as ANY God can make ANY Marvel from their Purview. :/ I was hoping for making Boon like emulating other Purviews Boons by extensive rituals or to counter other Boons \u2013 but with Marvels mechanics it\u2019s just loose sense, in my POV. Maybe you have some way to put Magic as special Purview?<br /> <br /> <b>Example Gods: </b>Odin ( Aesir ), Thoth ( Djehuty - Netjar ), Veles ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">Bogi</a> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as Glamour says, the problem with a Magic Purview is that you don't need <i>a</i> Magic Purview, you need several hundred. There is no consistent idea of what 'magic' is from Pantheon to Pantheon, it is fundamentally defined by that specific cultural group. The methods of magic used by the different Pantheons are so fundamentally different, and do different things that it cannot easily be made into a single Purview.<br /> <br /> However, Pantheon Specific Purviews tend to be the realm of these special culturally specific areas of magic. The Norse PsP, Wyrd, is explicitly modeled after Sei\u00f0r as well as the pop-culture idea of runes having magical powers, and the Norse concept of an inexorable Fate. The Netjer PsP is similarly an expression of how the Egyptians understood 'magic' to work, and thus it is fundamentally different from how the Aesir and Vanir do it. Similarly with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann PsP.<br /> <br /> The idea of extensive rituals for magical purposes tends to be common, but how these work is so vastly different they cannot easily be expressed by the same Purview. For instance, a Glam Dicenn from Ireland and ceremonial invocation of a Kami in order to move them to a different shrine are so different they may as well be chairs and clouds. Once again, both of them are best represented by both Pantheon's PsP.<br /> <br /> The idea of 'counter magic' is not something shared by all cultures, and would not be at hope in most of the Pantheons of the world as well, that is the realm of very modern ideas. Sure, there are some counter-magic knives found for the Ashanti, but they're counter-magic because you stab them through the mouths of witches during judgements and executions so they are unable to speak as their mouth is full of knife and blood. Not really like a counter-spell, just blocking a Motif through a physical action.<br /> <br /> This really is just a problem of translation. 'Magic' is a word that creates false equivalencies. The similarities between two Pantheon's 'Magic' systems very frequently is only that we describe it as 'Magic' in English as they will have different functions, methods, purposes, social roles, social results, theological situations, implementations, visual appearances, literally everything about them will be different asides from the very basic idea that we call it 'magic' in English. Thoth and Odin both are doing wildly different things that are in no way comparable asides from the English speaking world deciding they would use the same word for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 01-10-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T17:22:23-08:00","id":1280003,"title":"","content":"As Glamourweaver already mention the archetype of knowledge seeker/giver is well represented in the Sage calling, even the Hunter calling can work in the &quot;hunt for knowledge&quot; sense. <br /> <br /> As for knowledge in a more elemental context more fitting for a purview ... hm, this is tentative so far but i could see someone taking the Artistry purview with a Teaching specialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T03:09:10-08:00","id":1280075,"title":"","content":"Our group has drafted up a few purveiws. We are running a twisted version of Scion where we are playing VTM vampires in the same world. Instead of disciplines vampires just got purveiws. I don't have those write ups on me but the big ones where <br /> Pestilence - calling down plagues and the like, kinda an anti health <br /> Dreams (we also reworked darkness as we don't like them being combined as they are) <br /> Mind - wanted to cover mind reading and mental manipulation somewhere <br /> Flesh - covers flesh warping and making flesh golems <br /> Mirrors/ reflections <br /> And lastly Dominion for controlling the land <br /> <br /> Some have a distinct vampire bent, but some we feel could be applied to other gods on demand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T06:44:00-08:00","id":1280090,"title":"","content":"Health already covers Pestilence within itself - it's basically just half of the Health purview.<br /> <br /> But then, if you're going for VTM vampires, reflecting real religious ideas isn't really on the table much anyway.<br /> <br /> As for Knowledge: can you present ideas of what Knowledge marvels might look like and do that aren't already covered by Sage, yeah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:33:25-08:00","id":1280103,"title":"","content":"Just to note, they\u2019re going to cover custom purview building (at least at the Hero level) in the Companion. Some are likely just a matter of combing aspects of different Purviews: for example a \u201cDesert\u201d Purview might combine the negative halves of Fertility and Prosperity, with some very limited applications of Sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T12:40:50-08:00","id":1280386,"title":"","content":"To echo others... Neither of these Purviews are in any way necessary. &quot;Knowledge&quot; - That's a Calling. You're thinking of the Sage Calling. It has Knacks. They're awesome. Seriously, don't disregard Knacks. The Sage Calling covers literally all your needs for &quot;I Am A Smarty&quot;. It's like when I saw people asking why there wasn't a &quot;I'm strong enough to solo an army&quot; Boon in War. That's a Knack, you're not demonstrating a mythic connection with war and armies by beating them all up, you're a Warrior using a Knack.<br /> <br /> As for Magic, Watcher and Glamour have said it with many words. To put it in a shorter format: You have Marvels and Pantheon Motifs to represent cultural outlooks on magic, which shockingly is not as unified as many RPGs would like to say it is. If you MUST make a Magic Purview it would only realistically be through powers that improve Marvels, and it's probably not something I'd allow at my table without a good reason.<br /> <br /> Specifically, a good reason that DOESN'T sound like the player is trying to be a total munchkin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T19:07:34-08:00","id":1280431,"title":"","content":"I mean he started off saying Marvels make the presence of a Magic purview unnecessary. That should have been the end of it right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T21:00:45-08:00","id":1280440,"title":"","content":"I think about putting PsP in particular God's preview then, with speciality (Magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T21:03:12-08:00","id":1280441,"title":"","content":"Pantheon Specific Purviews are automatically in a God's purview and as said they already represent the magic of the culture connected.<br /> <br /> So that's literally how the game already works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T22:33:11-08:00","id":1280445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews?p=1280441#post1280441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pantheon Specific Purviews are automatically in a God's purview and as said they already represent the magic of the culture connected.<br /> <br /> So that's literally how the game already works.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the moral, kids, is RTFM.<br /> <br /> Even a specialty of Magic is unnecessary. The God in question just weaves many Marvels","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-13-2019, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T07:50:26-08:00","id":1280475,"title":"","content":"Whether or not a Knowledge purview is covered by the Sage calling, the lack of it got me thinking. Suppose there used to be a Primordial of Knowledge but for some reason, it retracted the knowledge of its own existence. No one, mortal or divine, remembers the Primordial used to be a thing. There may be a few hints about it that didn\u2019t get cleaned up when the Primordial withdrew, but people just say, \u201cLook how primitive that culture was! They believed there was actually a Knowledge Purview, when it was just the Sage calling.\u201d (Yes, I know people in the World don\u2019t literally talk about Purviews and Callings, but you know what I mean.)<br /> <br /> Of course, the question is why the Primordial withdrew. What Knowledge did it have that made it say, \u201cI have to erase myself from the World\u201d? And what slip-ups did it make that will allow a band of Scions to follow a trail of bread crumbs and learn the truth? Who else knows what\u2019s going on, and what will they do to prevent other people from gaining such precious Knowledge? What will change if the Primordial\u2019s deception is discovered? And what does it do to a Primordial of Knowledge if it acts against itself to *destroy* knowledge?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m now thinking that for my campaign, Atlantis relied on Knowledge to such an extent that when the Primordial withdrew, everything fell to pieces. So the trail of bread crumbs may start with my players finding themselves in Atlantis, and discovering some strange anomalies. One way or another, this is going to turn into a major story arc for my group. \u2014Jim Gardner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T02:27:41-08:00","id":1280651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews?p=1280475#post1280475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Yes, I know people in the World don\u2019t literally talk about Purviews and Callings, but you know what I mean.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>really</i> don't.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea of an Ancient Primordial withdrawing from even the Overworld and takings a great deal of knowledge with it is an interesting one, certainly, but there's no reason to tie it into any kind of Knowledge Purview. Especially as Primordials can have Callings. In fact, several do, such as Kitchi Manitou. Not EVERYTHING needs to be a Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:05:14-08:00","id":1280718,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not completely opposed to a knowedge Purview. Obviously Purviews and Callings can overlap (Deception and Trickster, Journeys and Liminal, Health and Healer). But i\u2019m going to need example Boons and Marvels that the Knowledge Purview can accomplish that are beyond the Sage Calling and within the role of knowledge Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:12:29-08:00","id":1280721,"title":"","content":"It might be interesting to have a Data purview for a Modern god or even a Pantheon Specific Purview for a tech Pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T20:10:50-08:00","id":1280817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews?p=1280721#post1280721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be interesting to have a Data purview for a Modern god or even a Pantheon Specific Purview for a tech Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m tinkering with an American Gods inspired setting Shard (would not use these ideas for the World, as that setting by design lacks a new vs old dichotomy, the Old Gods have kept up) and something like that is my idea for Novus Ordo Seclorum\u2019s PSP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T02:08:11-08:00","id":1281759,"title":"","content":"I have been thinking about the idea of an Light Purview, to encompass more specific light themes not sun/moon related: Illumination, healing light, vision, truth, blinding, being fast and essentially instantaneous, etc.<br /> <br /> Specially a boon I have in mind of being able to &quot;phase into light&quot; for an instant, allowing the character to pass through transparent glass (or shoot through glass), punch or pass through grids (like chain-mail) and move through long tubes straight tubes like light. I also imagine one that cleans illusions or reveals secretes/hidden objects, and also some innate power ability to turn on/off light and control luminosity.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think it is a worth purview to make or it is better as just a specialization of sun?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your attention, have a good day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T05:36:31-08:00","id":1281767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews?p=1281759#post1281759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been thinking about the idea of an Light Purview, to encompass more specific light themes not sun/moon related: Illumination, healing light, vision, truth, blinding, being fast and essentially instantaneous, etc.<br /> <br /> Specially a boon I have in mind of being able to &quot;phase into light&quot; for an instant, allowing the character to pass through transparent glass (or shoot through glass), punch or pass through grids (like chain-mail) and move through long tubes straight tubes like light. I also imagine one that cleans illusions or reveals secretes/hidden objects, and also some innate power ability to turn on/off light and control luminosity.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think it is a worth purview to make or it is better as just a specialization of sun?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your attention, have a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's hard to work into a Purview that would then be distributed to existing deities as well, since that is a very scientific, and not a mythological way of viewing light. Jumping off Sun and specialising it via Marvels etc. to make a new, modern deity of modern conceptions of light makes more sense, at least to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:33:31-08:00","id":1281808,"title":"","content":"Yeah, something to keep in mind with Purviews... You're often not looking at the literal modern scientific versions. Like the Darkness Purview isn't just about literal shadow and dark, it's also sleep, night, and dreams.<br /> <br /> Scientifically, sleep and dreams have nothing to do with Darkness.<br /> <br /> But symbolically, they have a link through Dark = Night = Sleep = Dreaming.<br /> <br /> So the Sun isn't just about the Blazing Ball of Gas up above. It IS Light, Warmth, the Baleful Gaze That Dispels Falsehood. It's the SYMBOLIC Sun.<br /> <br /> So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12934_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12934\" data-vbnamecard=\"12934\">Manbat</a> you can probably get by with just custom Boons in the Sun Purview. Maybe when the Companion hits you can see the rules for Specific Purviews to use &quot;Sun (Light)&quot;, like someone may use Fire (Volcanos) or Water (River)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:53:52-08:00","id":1281812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1279952-2e-new-purviews?p=1281759#post1281759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been thinking about the idea of an Light Purview, to encompass more specific light themes not sun/moon related: Illumination, healing light, vision, truth, blinding, being fast and essentially instantaneous, etc.<br /> <br /> Specially a boon I have in mind of being able to &amp;quot;phase into light&amp;quot; for an instant, allowing the character to pass through transparent glass (or shoot through glass), punch or pass through grids (like chain-mail) and move through long tubes straight tubes like light. I also imagine one that cleans illusions or reveals secretes/hidden objects, and also some innate power ability to turn on/off light and control luminosity.<br /> <br /> Do you guys think it is a worth purview to make or it is better as just a specialization of sun?<br /> <br /> Thank you for your attention, have a good day.</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201cZohar\u201d Purview i\u2019m fiddling with as the Mal\u2019akhim PSP touches on some of these concepts. And yeah, there is thematic overlap with Sun, but Wyrd overlaps with Fortune, Metamorphosis with Beast, Tianming with Order, etc - so i\u2019ve decided not to sweat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}